## Database (Entity Framework Core)

- Use EF Core's type-safe queries; avoid raw SQL unless necessary.
- Always use async/await for all database operations (`FirstOrDefaultAsync`, `SaveChangesAsync`).
- Use `Include()` for related entities when needed.
- Use `Select()` to only fetch needed fields for performance.
- Handle database errors gracefully with user-friendly messages.

## Migrations

- Always create migrations for schema changes.
- Use descriptive migration names.
- Never edit existing migrations (create new ones).
- Test migrations on development before applying to production.

## Repository pattern

- DbContext is registered as Scoped.
- Use services for business logic, not controllers.
- Configure relationships in `OnModelCreating()` in DbContext.

## Common patterns

```csharp
// Good - async with error handling
var user = await _context.Users
    .Include(u => u.Roles)
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(u => u.Id == userId);

if (user == null)
    return NotFound(new { message = "User not found" });

// Good - select only needed fields
var users = await _context.Users
    .Select(u => new UserDto { Id = u.Id, Email = u.Email })
    .ToListAsync();
```
